---
source: crates/observed_macros_impl/tests/expansion.rs
expression: output
---
---- input ----
#[event("e")]
#[gauge] struct Subject { #[unredacted] v: u64 }

---- yields ----
`#[gauge(...)]` requires a field naming the struct field that holds the metric value, e.g. `#[gauge(duration_ms)]`

---- input ----
#[event("e")]
#[histogram] struct Subject { #[unredacted] v: u64 }

---- yields ----
`#[histogram(...)]` requires a field naming the struct field that holds the metric value, e.g. `#[histogram(duration_ms)]`

---- input ----
#[event("e")]
#[updown_counter] struct Subject { #[unredacted] v: u64 }

---- yields ----
`#[updown_counter(...)]` requires a field naming the struct field that holds the metric value, e.g. `#[updown_counter(duration_ms)]`

---- input ----
#[event("e")]
#[counter] #[counter] struct Subject { #[unredacted] v: u64 }

---- yields ----
only one event-level metric (a fieldless `#[counter]`) is allowed

---- input ----
#[event("e")]
#[counter(absent)] struct Subject { #[unredacted] v: u64 }

---- yields ----
`#[counter(absent)]` references field `absent`, which does not exist in the struct

---- input ----
#[event("e")]
#[counter = "x"] struct Subject { #[unredacted] v: u64 }

---- yields ----
a metric attribute takes an optional field and `name`/`desc`/`unit` options, not `= value`

---- input ----
#[event("e")]
#[counter(v, bogus = "x")] struct Subject { #[unredacted] v: u64 }

---- yields ----
unknown metric option `bogus`; expected `name`, `desc`, or `unit`

---- input ----
#[event("e")]
#[counter(v, name = "a", name = "b")] struct Subject { #[unredacted] v: u64 }

---- yields ----
duplicate `name` setting

---- input ----
#[event("e")]
#[counter(v, desc = "a", desc = "b")] struct Subject { #[unredacted] v: u64 }

---- yields ----
duplicate `desc` setting

---- input ----
#[event("e")]
#[counter(v, unit = "a", unit = "b")] struct Subject { #[unredacted] v: u64 }

---- yields ----
duplicate `unit` setting

---- input ----
#[event("e")]
#[counter(v)] #[counter(v)] struct Subject { #[unredacted] v: u64 }

---- yields ----
field `v` already has a metric instrument
